        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "Medication overuse headache secondary to frequent simple analgesic and triptan use on a background of migraine without aura"
        },
        "clinicalStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-clinical",
              "code": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "verificationStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-ver-status",
              "code": "confirmed"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Condition/condition-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Condition",
        "id": "condition-2",
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "code": {
          "text": "High-frequency migraine without aura, suboptimally controlled due to medication overuse headache"
        },
        "clinicalStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-clinical",
              "code": "active"
            }
          ]
        },
        "verificationStatus": {
          "coding": [
            {
              "system": "http://terminology.hl7.org/CodeSystem/condition-ver-status",
              "code": "confirmed"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-1",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-1",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Headache frequency and pattern"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "History of migraine since late teens, previously 1–2 episodes per month. Over the last 4–5 months, headaches have occurred most days, with a baseline dull, band-like ache most days and superimposed typical migraine 1–2 times per week. The migraine character is otherwise unchanged, with increased frequency and background daily pain."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-2",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-2",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Typical migraine features"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Historically right-sided throbbing headache associated with photophobia and nausea; previously relieved by sumatriptan."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-3",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-3",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Headache response after analgesia"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports feeling okay for a few hours after tablets, then the headache returns as the tablets wear off, sometimes worse, typically 4–6 hours after a dose. Often wakes with a mild headache several mornings per week, takes analgesia mid-morning, improves, then the headache returns in the late afternoon or evening."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-4",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-4",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Headache-associated and red-flag symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies thunderclap onset, worst-ever headache, focal neurological symptoms, speech disturbance, limb weakness, visual loss, fever, neck stiffness, head trauma, seizures, personality change, weight loss, and nocturnal headache waking her."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-5",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-5",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sleep"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Sleeps 6–7 hours per night, often interrupted by young children."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Caffeine intake"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Drinks 2–3 coffees per day. Patient wonders whether too much coffee may be making the headaches worse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Screen and workplace lighting concern"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient wonders whether staring at the screen in poor office lighting may be making the headaches worse."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Mood and psychological symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Feels a bit worn down by constant pain. Denies pervasive low mood, anhedonia, anxiety attacks, and suicidal ideation."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Paracetamol use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports taking paracetamol 1 g with ibuprofen 400 mg most days, pretty much every day after lunch and often again at night, estimated at 20 or more days per month. Medication list states paracetamol 1 g up to every 6 hours as needed, currently 2–3 doses most days."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Ibuprofen use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Reports taking ibuprofen 400 mg with paracetamol most days, estimated at 20 or more days per month. Medication list states ibuprofen 400 mg up to three times daily as needed, often 1–2 doses per day."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Sumatriptan use"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Uses sumatriptan 50 mg as needed for migraine, approximately 8–10 days per month."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
